 binning shows the events fire out of order: 96-2599 (~83.6k) precedes 2853-96 (~83.9k), and 7205-5573 (~84.3k) precedes 2599-7205 (~84.5k). Each of these edges has exactly one event in the window, so no alternative ordering exists, and 4243/5573 each have degree 1, so no alternative route exists. No time-respecting, Delta<=600 chain can carry influence from 4243 to 5573."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static path (ignoring time):** 4243 \u2192 2853 \u2192 96 \u2192 2599 \u2192 7205 \u2192 5573 (steps 03\u201305). This is the *only* route \u2014 4243 has exactly 1 event and 1 partner in the window, 5573 likewise (step_02), and the k-hop closures are tiny and non-truncated.\n\n**Temporal localization of each required hop** (steps 06\u201316):\n\n| hop | time bin |\n|---|---|\n| 4243\u20132853 | 83393\u201383492 |\n| 96\u20132599 | 83593\u201383692 |\n| 2853\u201396 | 83893\u201383992 |\n| 7205\u20135573 | 84293\u201384392 |\n| 2599\u20137205 | 84493\u201384592 |\n\n**Two ordering violations break the chain:**\n- 96\u21922599 (~83.6k) fires *before* 2853\u219296 (~83.9k). The only 96\u20132599 contact is already in the past when 96 is reached.\n- 7205\u21925573 (~84.3k) fires *before* 2599\u21927205 (~84.5k). The only delivery to 5573 precedes 7205's activation.\n\nSince each of these edges has exactly one event in the window (steps 08, 14, 15, 16), there is no alternative timing. The \u0394\u2264600 constraint is never even reached as a binding factor \u2014 the sequence fails monotonicity first. The apparent connection is a pure static/aggregation artifact.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_82acc9f1\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [4243, 2853, 96, 2599, 7205, 5573],\n  \"window\": [79193, 88793],\n  \"confidence\": 0.86,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A single static path 4243-2853-96-2599-7205-5573 exists, and all its activity is packed into ~1200 time units, which superficially looks cascade-like. But fine-grained binning shows the events fire out of order: 96-2599 (~83.6k) precedes 2853-96 (~83.9k), and 7205-5573 (~84.3k) precedes 2599-7205 (~84.5k). Each of these edges has exactly one event in the window, so no alternative ordering exists, and 4243/5573 each have degree 1, so no alternative route exists. No time-respecting, Delta<=600 chain can carry influence from 4243 to 5573.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 34205, "total_output_tokens": 7793, "total_tokens": 41998, "total_latency_ms": 95829, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}